    <string name="automatic_forwarding_new_sms_is_sent_automatically_when_enabled_w">"Automatic forwarding\nNew SMS is sent automatically when enabled. While paused, new messages stay on the phone and resume when enabled again. Your existing inbox is not imported.\n\nSending failures\nMost network errors are retried later. You can also choose “Retry unsent SMS”.\n\nCheck email delivery\nIf the connection drops during sending, the app may not know whether an email was sent. To avoid duplicates, it will not retry automatically. Check your inbox and spam folder, then choose “Received” or “Not received, resend”.\n\nSwitching profiles\nTap a card to switch; choose “Edit profile” to change it. Emails that have started sending keep their original recipient. Switch back to that profile to resume them.\n\nBackground activity\nIf forwarding is delayed, allow background activity in system battery settings. Open the app again after force-stopping it."</string>
